ems: center; gap: 20px;\" target=\"_blank\"> <svg class=\"download_svg\" fill=\"none\" height=\"65\" viewbox=\"0 0 65 65\" width=\"65\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"> <path d=\"M34.7087 0.802246L51.9921 16.7998V63.2344C51.9921 64.0948 51.2946 64.7922 50.4342 64.7922H2.24001C1.37961 64.7922 0.682129 64.0948 0.682129 63.2344V2.36012C0.682129 1.49973 1.37961 0.802246 2.24001 0.802246H34.7087Z\" fill=\"#2172D0\" fill-rule=\"evenodd\"></path> <path d=\"M2.89377 4.57204C2.89377 3.71164 3.59125 3.01416 4.45165 3.01416H33.4957C33.9151 3.01416 34.3168 3.18328 34.6099 3.48327L41.4271 10.46L49.2189 16.9423C49.5747 17.2383 49.7804 17.6771 49.7804 18.1399V61.023C49.7804 61.8834 49.083 62.5809 48.2226 62.5809H4.45164C3.59125 62.5809 2.89377 61.8834 2.89377 61.023V4.57204Z\" fill=\"white\"></path> <path d=\"M34.6774 18.3479H51.9922L33.1196 0.802246V16.79C33.1196 17.6504 33.8171 18.3479 34.6774 18.3479Z\" fill=\"#2172D0\"></path> <rect fill=\"#2172D0\" height=\"2.99978\" width=\"9.99928\" x=\"8.99524\" y=\"16.801\"></rect> <rect fill=\"#2172D0\" height=\"2.99978\" width=\"9.99928\" x=\"8.99524\" y=\"34.7998\"></rect> <rect fill=\"#2172D0\" height=\"2.99978\" width=\"23.9983\" x=\"8.99524\" y=\"25.8005\"></rect> <circle cx=\"44.9022\" cy=\"44.7086\" fill=\"white\" r=\"10.7622\" stroke=\"#2172D0\" stroke-width=\"2.47381\" transform=\"rotate(-49.859 44.9022 44.7086)\"></circle> <path d=\"M60.723 60.9036C61.7674 61.7844 63.3281 61.6517 64.2089 60.6073C65.0897 59.5628 64.957 58.0021 63.9126 57.1214L60.723 60.9036ZM52.2213 53.7341L60.723 60.9036L63.9126 57.1214L55.4109 49.9519L52.2213 53.7341Z\" fill=\"#2172D0\"></path> </svg> Application Instruction </a></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\"><!-- 第一条 -->\n<div class=\"pct_st-p\">\n<p class=\"pct_p\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"pct_st\"><strong>Overview<strong></strong></strong></h3>\nThe following models all require the use of a <strong>Power Distribution Board - 4 Channels.</strong> To complete the assembly of a full model, users need to download the model files and 3D print the remaining parts.\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_t-tb\">\n<table class=\"pct_tb\" style=\"width: 100.061%; height: 78.3752px;\"><!-- 表头 -->\n<tbody><!-- 第一行 --><!-- 第二行 -->\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\" style=\"height: 19.5938px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 39.7009%; height: 19.5938px;\"><strong>Models Using This Part</strong></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 14.2304%; height: 19.5938px;\"><strong>Creators</strong></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 42.4863%; height: 19.5938px;\"><b>Model Links</b></td>\n</tr>\n<!-- 第三行 -->\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\" style=\"height: 19.5938px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 39.7009%; height: 19.5938px;\">\n<div data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\" data-page-id=\"OKsfdVZTpoQRnExo2lIcyoskncC\">\n<div class=\"old-record-id-WN9wdvxjroLLKUxZrwrcWzjZnhd\">Endless Loop Express</div>\n</div>\n<span class=\"lark-record-clipboard\" data-lark-record-data='{\"rootId\":\"OKsfdVZTpoQRnExo2lIcyoskncC\",\"text\":{\"initialAttributedTexts\":{\"text\":{\"0\":\"Button\"},\"attribs\":{\"0\":\"*0+6\"}},\"apool\":{\"numToAttrib\":{\"0\":[\"author\",\"7118919285765865474\"]},\"nextNum\":1}},\"type\":\"text\",\"referenceRecordMap\":{},\"extra\":{\"mention_page_title\":{},\"external_mention_url\":{}},\"isKeepQuoteContainer\":false,\"isFromCode\":false,\"selection\":[{\"id\":64,\"type\":\"text\",\"selection\":{\"start\":0,\"end\":6},\"recordId\":\"WN9wdvxjroLLKUxZrwrcWzjZnhd\"}],\"payloadMap\":{},\"isCut\":false}' data-lark-record-format=\"docx/text\"></span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 14.2304%; height: 19.5938px;\">IMD_Q.</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 42.4863%; height: 19.5938px;\"><a href=\"https://makerworld.com/en/models/431820?from=search#profileId-348512\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong>Endless Loop Express</strong></span></a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\" style=\"height: 19.5938px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 39.7009%; height: 19.5938px;\">Running Dinosaur Automaton</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 14.2304%; height: 19.5938px;\"><span>Amao Chan</span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 42.4863%; height: 19.5938px;\"><a href=\"https://makerworld.com/zh/models/422534#profileId-325850\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\">Running Dinosaur Automaton</span></strong></a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\" style=\"height: 19.5938px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 39.7009%; height: 19.5938px;\">Mini Motorized Basketball Game</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 14.2304%; height: 19.5938px;\">Kit Crafters</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 42.4863%; height: 19.5938px;\"><a href=\"https://makerworld.com/zh/models/420464#profileId-323162\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong><span>Mini Motorized Basketball Game</span></strong></span></a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_padding-in-mobile\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_st\"></h2>\n<p> </p>\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\">Instruction</h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_st\"></h2>\n<p>The Power Distribution Board (PDB) - 4 Channels is used for connecting various electrical devices, switches, and power supplies, supporting electric devices up to 4 channels.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Use two M2 screws for fastening (unless otherwise specified, all fastening screws used for the kit's PCBA are M2 screws).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The IN is for connecting to various power supplies, such as a USB-A Power Cable with PH2.0 Connector or battery box. IN and OUT are interconnected, and OUT can be used to connect to another Potentiometer Board with SH1.0 Connector in series. IN/OUT uses a PH2.0-2P connector.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The SW0 to SW4 is used for connecting switches such as Potentiometer Board with SH1.0 Connector, Self-Locking Button Switch with SH1.0 Connector or Jumper Cable with SH1.0 Connector.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The CH1 to CH4 is used for connecting electrical devices such as N20 Reduction Gear Motor, 3030-LED Board with SH1.0 Connector, 2510 5V DC Fan with SH1.0 Connector, etc. Please do not connect the Potentiometer Board with SH1.0 Connector, Self-Locking Button Switch with SH1.0 Connector or Jumper Cable with SH1.0 Connector to these channels.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>SW0 is the master switch, while SW1 to SW4 are individual switches for controlling channels CH1 to CH4 respectively. The SW0 to SW4 uses a SH1.0-2P connector.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The LED indicator shows the system status. When the battery box and master switch are connected, the LED lights up white, indicating normal status. If the total current exceeds 1A or if a short circuit occurs in any of the CH1 to CH4 channels, the current-limiting chip will cut off the power supply, and the LED will turn off. After the overcurrent or short-circuit condition is removed, the power supply will remain disconnected. To restore normal operation, the main switch must be turned off and then reconnected.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Please do not connect switches to the CH1 to CH4, and avoid connecting electrical devices to SW1 to SW4 as this may cause a short circuit.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_padding-in-mobile\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\"></h2>\n<p> </p>\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\">Electronics System</h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_st\"></h2>\n<p>The components of this circuit set can be divided into five categories: <a href=\"../../../products/power-distribution-board-pdb-4-channels\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong>Power Distribution Board (PDB) - 4 Channels</strong></span></span></a><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">,</span> power-type devices, power supply devices, switch devices, and wires. The Power Distribution Board has channels for connecting power supply devices, switch devices, and electric devices. Please refer to the figure below for the devices supported by each connector. The IN is used to connect various power supply devices, such as <a href=\"../../../products/battery-case-with-ph2-0-connector\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong>AA Battery Case</strong></span></span></a> and <a href=\"products/usb-a-power-cable-with-ph2-0-connector\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong>USB-A Power Cable</strong></span></span></a>; the CH1-4 are used to connect various electrical devices, such as <a href=\"../../../products/n20-reduction-gear-motor\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong>N20 Reduction Gear Motor (150rpm)</strong></span></span></a> and <a href=\"../../../products/3030-5v-led-board-with-sh1-0-connector\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong>4 White 3030-LED Board</strong></span></span></a>, and supports up to 4 connections; the SW0~4 is used to connect various switch devices, such as <a href=\"../../../products/self-locking-button-switch-with-sh1-0-connector\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong>Self-locking Button Switch</strong></span></span></a><a href=\"https://asia.store.bambulab.com/products/power-distribution-board-pdb-4-channelsbambulab.com/products/self-locking-button-switch-with-sh1-0-connector\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">, </a><a href=\"../../../products/potentiometer-board-with-sh1-0-connector\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\">Potentiometer Board</span></strong></span></a>, and <a href=\"../../../products/jumper-cable-with-sh1-0-connector\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong>Jumper Cable</strong></span></span></a>. Please do not connect electric devices to the SW0~4, and likewise, do not connect switches to the CH1~4. The OUT is used to connect to the next Power Distribution Board to achieve connector expansion. To learn more about the case, please refer to the<a href=\"https://store.bblcdn.com/s1/default/ac88b934066a4265854fa49b98160c5f.zip\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"> <span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong>Application Instruction</strong></span></a>.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_st-tbc product-specification-table-small-padding\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\"></h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_st\"></h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\">Product Specifications</h2>\n<div class=\"pct_tbc\">\n<table class=\"pct_tb\" style=\"border-color: #adadad; font-weight: bold; height: 74px;\"><!-- 表头 -->\n<thead class=\"pct_th\">\n<tr style=\"height: 55px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #adadad; font-weight: bold; text-align: center; height: 55px; width: 72.4574px;\">\n<div>Product ID</div>\n</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #adadad; font-weight: bold; height: 55px; width: 148.139px;\">\n<div>Maximum Current</div>\n<p>(A)</p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #adadad; font-weight: bold; height: 55px; width: 148.04px;\">\n<div>Maximum Voltage\n<p>(V)</p>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #adadad; font-weight: bold; height: 55px; width: 76.733px;\">\n<div>Size\n<div>\n<p>(mm)</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #adadad; font-weight: bold; height: 55px; width: 72.5284px;\">\n<div>Weight</div>\n<p>(g)</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\" style=\"height: 19px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #adadad; text-align: center; height: 19px; width: 72.4574px;\">IA005</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #adadad; height: 19px; width: 148.139px;\">1A</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #adadad; height: 19px; width: 148.04px;\">7.4V</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #adadad; height: 19px; width: 76.733px;\">53x10x10</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #adadad; height: 19px; width: 72.5284px;\">3</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_st-tbc product-specification-table-small-padding\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\"></h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_st\"></h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\">Connector Model</h2>\n<div class=\"pct_tbc\">\n<table class=\"pct_tb\" style=\"border-color: #ADADAD; font-weight: bold;\"><!-- 表头 -->\n<thead class=\"pct_th\">\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #ADADAD; font-weight: bold; text-align: center;\">\n<div>Input</div>\n</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #ADADAD; font-weight: bold;\">\n<div>Output</div>\n</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #ADADAD; font-weight: bold;\">\n<div>SW0-4</div>\n</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #ADADAD; font-weight: bold;\">\n<div>CH1-4</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #ADADAD; text-align: center;\">PH2.0-2P</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #ADADAD;\">PH2.0-2P</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #ADADAD;\">SH1.0-2P</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #ADADAD;\">SH1.0-2P</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_padding-in-mobile\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\"></h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_st\"></h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\">In the box</h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_st\"></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Power Distribution Board (PDB) x1pcs</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>USB-A Power Cable with PH2.0 Connector x1pcs</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Wire Pair with PH2.0 x1pcs</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Jumper Cable with SH1.0 Connector x5pcs</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_padding-in-mobile\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\"></h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_st\"></h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\">Consideration</h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_st\"></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Please do not forcefully twist the connectors to avoid wires loosening or detaching.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>",
  "description_text": "The Power Distribution Board (PDB) - 4 Channels is used for connecting various electrical devices, switches, and power supplies, supporting electric devices up to 4 channels.\n\nUse two M2 screws for fastening (unless otherwise specified, all fastening screws used for the kit's PCBA are M2 screws).\n\nThe IN is for connecting to various power supplies, such as a USB-A Power Cable with PH2.0 Connector or battery box. IN and OUT are interconnected, and OUT can be used to connect to another Potentiometer Board with SH1.0 Connector in series. IN/OUT uses a PH2.0-2P connector.\n\nThe SW0 to SW4 is used for connecting switches such as Potentiometer Board with SH1.0 Connector, Self-Locking Button Switch with SH1.0 Connector or Jumper Cable with SH1.0 Connector.\n\nThe CH1 to CH4 is used for connecting electrical devices such as N20 Reduction Gear Motor, 3030-LED Board with SH1.0 Connector, 2510 5V DC Fan with SH1.0 Connector, etc. Please do not connect the Potentiometer Board with SH1.0 Connector, Self-Locking Button Switch with SH1.0 Connector or Jumper Cable with SH1.0 Connector to these channels.\n\nSW0 is the master switch, while SW1 to SW4 are individual switches for controlling channels CH1 to CH4 respectively. The SW0 to SW4 uses a SH1.0-2P connector.\n\nThe LED indicator shows the system status. When the battery box and master switch are connected, the LED lights up white, indicating normal status. If the total current exceeds 1A or if a short circuit occurs in any of the CH1 to CH4 channels, the current-limiting chip will cut off the power supply, and the LED will turn off. After the overcurrent or short-circuit condition is removed, the power supply will remain disconnected. To restore normal operation, the main switch must be turned off and then reconnected.\n\nPlease do not connect switches to the CH1 to CH4, and avoid connecting electrical devices to SW1 to SW4 as this may cause a short circuit.\n\nThe components of this circuit set can be divided into five categories: Power Distribution Board (PDB) - 4 Channels, power-type devices, power supply devices, switch devices, and wires. The Power Distribution Board has channels for connecting power supply devices, switch devices, and electric devices. Please refer to the figure below for the devices supported by each connector. The IN is used to connect various power supply devices, such as AA Battery Case and USB-A Power Cable; the CH1-4 are used to connect various electrical devices, such as N20 Reduction Gear Motor (150rpm) and 4 White 3030-LED Board, and supports up to 4 connections; the SW0~4 is used to connect various switch devices, such as Self-locking Button Switch, Potentiometer Board, and Jumper Cable. Please do not connect electric devices to the SW0~4, and likewise, do not connect switches to the CH1~4. The OUT is used to connect to the next Power Distribution Board to achieve connector expansion. To learn more about the case, please refer to the Application Instruction.\n\nPlease do not forcefully twist the connectors to avoid wires loosening or detaching.",
